Hi Chris,

I'm not super familiar with this object class, but I think you need levels=1-exp(-1) to fix to the Argos sqrt(2)-standard-error ellipse format, which then lets you drop the sqrt(2) from your code later on, because I suspect your ell.info <http://ell.info> object is not the 1-standard-error COV-matrix ellipse, but the ellipse with coverage levels.

For the angles, try this code:

u <- eigen.info <http://eigen.info>$vectors[,1] # major axis eigenvector
theta <- atan2(u[2],u[1]) # angle from x-axis in radians
theta <- theta *360/(2*pi) # angle from x-axis in degrees
theta <- theta - 90 # angle from y-axis in degrees

I forgot to mention that Argos format is in degrees.

Best,
Chris

